# LIGHT desktop package set — Libre Computer Le/La Frite (Amlogic arm64)
#
# A LEAN desktop, NOT the full Plasma+gaming stage4. Appended to packages.list by
# build-frite-stage4.sh when --desktop light (the DEFAULT for this target) is set.
# Sized for a low-end SBC (512 MB / 1 GB DDR4, Mali-450): X11 + a lightweight WM +
# a panel + a file manager + a terminal + a minimal browser. No KDE/GNOME/Plasma,
# no compositor-heavy Wayland session, no gaming stack.
#
# Picked for arm64 cross-friendliness + small footprint. If a 512 MB board feels
# tight, drop the browser line (or swap for a lighter one) — see RUNNING.md.

# ── Display server (X11; lean) ─────────────────────────────────────
x11-base/xorg-server
x11-apps/xrandr
x11-apps/xset
x11-apps/setxkbmap
x11-misc/xterm

# ── Desktop session: LXDE-lite (PCManFM + Openbox + LXpanel) ───────
# LXDE is the canonical "lean desktop": GTK-based, no compositor required, runs
# comfortably in well under the Frite's RAM. Openbox is the WM; lxpanel the panel;
# pcmanfm the file manager; lxsession ties the session together.
x11-wm/openbox
lxde-base/lxpanel
lxde-base/lxsession
lxde-base/pcmanfm
lxde-base/lxappearance

# ── Login / session bring-up ───────────────────────────────────────
# LightDM is the lean display manager; on a single-user appliance you can also
# autostart Openbox from .xinitrc and drop lightdm — see RUNNING.md.
x11-misc/lightdm
x11-misc/lightdm-gtk-greeter

# ── Minimal apps ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
media-gfx/feh
app-editors/nano
# A minimal, modern browser. NetSurf is dramatically lighter than Chromium/
# Firefox and cross-compiles cleanly for arm64 — appropriate for a 512MB SBC.
# Swap for www-client/firefox-bin only on the 1 GB SKU if a full browser is
# required (it is HEAVY — see the SKU note in RUNNING.md).
www-client/netsurf

# ── Fonts (so the lean desktop is legible out of the box) ──────────
media-fonts/dejavu
media-fonts/noto
